		{
			description: [
				"Exposure cameras, maps and written books let the group preserve discoveries beyond a waypoint name. Photograph rare creatures, dramatic terrain and completed builds from deliberate angles."
				"Create a museum or archive with dates, locations and short captions. Future players should understand why an ordinary-looking object mattered to the original expedition."
				"A world becomes a shared story when evidence of earlier journeys survives the players who made them."
				"A creative expedition should return with more than screenshots: develop an album, label an object, write the route, and explain one mechanic. Art becomes field knowledge when it helps the next player understand the place."
			]
